questions.answer:
For a long line charge,
\[
E=\frac{\lambda}{2\pi\epsilon_0r}
\]
\[
E=\frac{3.0\times10^{-9}}{2\pi(8.85\times10^{-12})(0.050)}
\]
\[
E=1.08\times10^3\,\mathrm{N\,C^{-1}}
\]

For an infinite sheet,
\[
E=\frac{\sigma}{2\epsilon_0}
\]
\[
E=\frac{4.0\times10^{-9}}{2(8.85\times10^{-12})}
\]
\[
E=2.26\times10^2\,\mathrm{N\,C^{-1}}
\]

Inside a uniformly charged solid sphere,
\[
E=\frac{1}{4\pi\epsilon_0}\frac{Qr}{R^3}
\]
\[
E=(8.99\times10^9)\frac{(8.0\times10^{-9})(0.10)}{(0.20)^3}
\]
\[
E=8.99\times10^2\,\mathrm{N\,C^{-1}}
\]
